content.thinking:
Repository compiles. Now implement WaterService — the core. Key pieces:

1. Validation helpers: requireNonBlank, parseVolume (BigDecimal, scale ≤ 3, > 0, normalize scale 3), parseInstant.
2. Idempotent command wrapper using TransactionTemplate.
3. Business logic per operation.

Idempotency wrapper design:

```java
private <T> T runCommand(String commandKey, String operation, Object params, Class<T> type, Supplier<T> action) {
    String key = requireNonBlank(commandKey, "commandKey");
    String paramsHash = hash(operation, params);
    CommandRecord existing = repository.findCommand(key);
    if (existing != null) {
        return replay(existing, operation, paramsHash, type);
    }
    try {
        return transactionTemplate.execute(status -> {
            T result = action.get();
            String body = toJson(result);
            repository.insertCommand(key, operation, paramsHash, 200, body, nowMs());
            return result;
        });
    } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
        CommandRecord concurrent = repository.findCommand(key);
        if (concurrent == null) throw ...; // shouldn't happen
        return replay(concurrent, operation, paramsHash, type);
    }
}
```

Wait: http_status stored — replay should return stored status. For create ops status is 201, others 200. Controller decides status... but replay returns stored body; the controller will return the same status for replay as for fresh? If controller always returns 201 for createWindow regardless of fresh/replay, then stored status is redundant but fine. "同键同参重放返回首次结果" — returning 201 + same body on replay is returning the first result. So controller can use fixed status codes per endpoint, and I don't need to store http_status (but schema has it; keep storing for fidelity).

But there's a subtlety: how does the service signal replay vs fresh? Not needed if status is fixed per endpoint. Good — simpler.

params for hash: include operation name + all request params (including path vars and actor). I'll serialize the params object with Jackson ObjectMapper (deterministic for records — field order is declaration order, stable). Compute SHA-256 hex of operation + "\n" + json.

Transaction: use TransactionTemplate (PlatformTransactionManager). The findCommand before tx is a plain read. Inside tx: action + insertCommand. On DuplicateKeyException from insertCommand — H2/MySQL — the tx will roll back; TransactionTemplate.execute propagates the exception after rollback. Catch outside, re-read, replay or 409.

Note: action.get() may throw ApiException → propagates, tx rolls back, no command record stored → retry allowed. Good.

replay: if !existing.operation().equals(operation) || !existing.paramsHash().equals(paramsHash) → throw conflict("COMMAND_CONFLICT", ...). Else deserialize body to type.

Business actions:

createWindow:
